# default.conf is rendered from default.conf.template by entrypoint.sh
default.conf

# certbot/letsencrypt is populated by hooks/pre-install.sh at deploy time — it
# copies from the sibling .secrets/letsencrypt/ into this build context because
# docker build refuses to follow symlinks outside of its context directory.
certbot/letsencrypt/

# Everything under frontend/ stays TRACKED — no blanket ignore here.
#
# frontend/docs is the Swagger UI bundle the image serves at /docs/
# (Dockerfile: COPY ./frontend/docs /var/www/docs). Ignoring frontend/ wholesale,
# as ocpp-css and plugme used to, left a fresh clone with nothing for that COPY
# to find. The api.yaml inside it is generated per brand by tools/mk-openapi.py
# in the platform workspace.
#
# frontend/php — a dead contact-form mailer carrying a plaintext SMTP password —
# was deleted from the build context on 2026-08-06, together with the php-fpm
# packages and their startup in entrypoint.sh. No ignore rule is left behind on
# purpose: if that directory ever reappears it should show up in `git status`,
# not be hidden.
